    <div class="eyebrow">Buy Better Finds Standards</div>
    <h1>Buy Better Finds Standards</h1>
    <p class="lead">Our standards explain how we research products, compare alternatives, evaluate tradeoffs, and build recommendations to help shoppers make more informed decisions.</p>

    <h2>01 — Research</h2>
    <p>We start with specific products and their intended use. We look for useful product information, core features, practical constraints, and the details that can materially change a buying decision.</p>

    <h2>02 — Compare</h2>
    <p>We consider alternatives where they make sense. Our comparisons focus on meaningful differences such as intended use, features, size, convenience, value, and limitations—not simply a higher specification count.</p>

    <h2>03 — Recommend</h2>
    <p>We explain who a product fits, what stands out, and what to watch before buying. A recommendation can be positive while still identifying clear reasons a different product may be a better fit for another shopper.</p>

    <h2>Buy Better Score</h2>
    <p>Our 10-point score is an editorial assessment, not a retailer rating. We consider five practical areas:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Use-case fit:</strong> how well the product matches the people and situations we identify.</li>
      <li><strong>Useful features:</strong> whether the features meaningfully support the intended use.</li>
      <li><strong>Practicality:</strong> convenience, setup, size, maintenance, or other real-world considerations.</li>
      <li><strong>Value:</strong> what the product offers relative to its price positioning and alternatives.</li>
      <li><strong>Tradeoffs:</strong> limitations, compatibility issues, recurring costs, or reasons to choose something else.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The score is a Buy Better Finds editorial judgment. It is not an Amazon customer rating, Amazon's Choice designation, or a guarantee of future performance.</p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. We may earn a commission when a qualifying purchase is made. Affiliate compensation does not determine a product's score or recommendation.</p>
    <p><strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong></p>

    <h2>Prices and availability</h2>
    <p>Retail prices, promotions, stock, shipping, warranties, and return policies can change. When we show a reference price or link to a retailer, verify the current details at checkout.</p>

    <h2>Images and sourcing</h2>
    <p>We prioritize manufacturer media resources, authorized press materials, original photography, and other imagery for which appropriate usage rights are established. New Daily Deal products are selected with verified official imagery or media-source documentation in mind.</p>

    <h2>Review cadence</h2>
    <p>Individual product pages show when their editorial assessment was last reviewed. We may revisit recommendations when product versions, meaningful alternatives, or other decision-relevant information changes.</p>

